MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_001: I've got to hide!
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_002: Over here, Miss Sha Lan!
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_003: Ah! Lian Ren?!
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_004: It appears the priests have gone. Apologies for\ngrabbing your arm like that.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_005: No, no, it's fine. Thank you for hiding me.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_006: It's a bit pathetic that I feel the need to hide\nwhenever I see a bunch of priests...
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_007: They're just doing their jobs. It isn't as if they're out\nhunting for those of the White Egg all the time.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_008: There's no need to frown like that, beautiful. You\nhave done nothing wrong.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_009: In fact, it is I who should express gratitude to you.\nPlease accept my sincerest thanks, Miss Sha Lan.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_010: Why are you thanking me?
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_011: You allowed me the great honor of rescuing a lovely\nlady, did you not?
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_012: You call me beautiful and lovely so casually... These\nwords that hold such weight...
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_013: Please excuse me. I'd intended them to be but a cool\nbreeze in your ear. Did they blow too hot for you?
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_014: Don't tease me. I know you're hitting on me.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_015: It's just that...you're special. You look so much like\nmy first love...
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_016: Do I? Is this the Lian Ren you called out to?
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_017: Ah, so you heard me say his name, then.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_018: He's older, kind, and tall...and he has a nice smile.\nThough I suppose you might be more handsome.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_019: Well, yes, of course I am. You would be hard-pressed\nto find anyone as beautiful...
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_020: Ah! I'm so sorry. Though I'm reluctant to leave you,\nI'd also hate to leave my date waiting and wanting.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_021: Oh, were you on your way to meet someone?\nI'm sorry for taking up so much of your time.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_022: It's fine. But if the quiet ever leaves you feeling\nlonely, please call upon the Fiery Wind. Goodbye.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_023: He is a kind person, it seems. Thoughtful too, asking\nme not to blame myself.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_C_024: What an intriguing traveler. And such a gentleman.\nAlmost makes it feel worth leaving Kunlun behind...
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_001: Miss Sha Lan! Free tonight? I can tell you the love\nstory of champion Breza! It's sure to make you melt.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_002: I can't believe you can say that with a straight face.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_003: Is something the matter? If I said something to\noffend you, that was not my intent...
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_004: You've been deceiving me! The traveler's attire you\nwear is to cover up the fact that you're a vulkan!
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_005: You sheltered me from those priests, when all the\nwhile, you were an agent of the temples yourself!
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_006: Oh, that's what this is about? It took you a while\nto realize.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_007: You're so wary, but you're like a baby bird, fluttering\ninnocently through the currents of air.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_008: You mock me! And here I thought you were kind\nand considerate...
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_009: I never want to see you again. Stay away from me!
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_010: Well, alright. Shame though. There was so much I\nyearned to talk about with you...
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_011: No more of your disingenuous poetical sputtering.\nI've had plenty. Go away.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_012: No, you misunderstand me. I wanted to find an\nopportunity to talk about sacred magic.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_013: As one of the People of the White Egg, you're not\naffiliated with any of the temples.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_014: So it is highly unusual—unnatural, even!—that you\nwould excel in the discipline.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_015: Much of what I know I taught myself. I base it off of\nthe principles of spirit magic.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_016: I wanted to do whatever I could to help those I\ncare for.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_017: I suspected as much. And with your purity of heart\ncomes no shortage of intelligence and cleverness.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_018: You must have worked tirelessly. I respect that\nstrength of will, regardless of my position.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_019: I see. I wouldn't have expected to hear that from\nsome temple big shot.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_020: That's why I said "regardless of my position."\nAnyway, I've only rustled your leaves. I'll get going.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_021: Good day, Miss Sha Lan. Apologies for the\ndiscomfort I caused.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_022: Hey, wait. You're leaving already?
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_023: *sigh* What is it I want from him, anyway?
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_024: First I think he's wonderful because he reminds me\nof Lian Ren, then I tell him to go away.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_B_025: Sirocco sees how hard I've worked. He sees me...
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_001: Hehe. Leave it to Kalla to quell every quarrel\nwith her poetry.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_002: Is that from the temple of Kalla's library?
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_003: Miss Sha Lan, you sought me out? I'm honored\nand humbled, truly.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_004: Don't talk to me like that. It's not like I've been\nignoring you.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_005: True, but I prefer to engage in fervent conversation,\nthat I might gaze upon your honest face.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_006: In that case, I have a request. One that will mean we\nhave more opportunities to talk.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_007: I'd like to learn about advanced sacred magic and\ntemples from you. You're well informed on the topics.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_008: I'm...rather taken aback. You want lessons from the\nman who deceived you?
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_009: Oh, stop. It's all fine, Sirocco.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_010: When I think of the history burned by Dagda, I feel\nmistrustful of the gods and their temples.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_011: My hatred of the temples can't be easily erased. But\nI can acknowledge that not all priests are enemies.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_012: I see. Well, anything to become better acquainted\nwith a beauty such as you.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_013: Ugh, again with the compliments.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_014: I once said you reminded me of Lian Ren, but I feel\nlike I'm going to have to rescind that statement.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_015: After all, unlike you, he only had eyes for me.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_016: It's true. As you appear to have finally noticed,\nI am a migratory creature.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_017: But my respect for you, and my desire to become\nyour friend, are entirely heartfelt, I assure you.
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_018: You are choosing to achieve your goals, despite\nyour desire not to speak to me. It's dazzling—noble!
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_019: And yes, if this is your wish, allow me to be the\nwind that fills your slightly reluctant sails!
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_020: Oh, you and your silvery words...
MID_SE_Sci_Sar_A_021: It almost makes me feel like letting you deceive me\nagain. Don't make me think such things.